#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0206 expect=skipped domain=ADSL
#note "THE SHAPE THIS PLAN GATES, PMDA arm. ADSL carries NO SEX while DM does. This rule reads 'not empty(SEX) and SEX != DM.SEX', so before the declaration it did not flood -- it was SILENTLY inert: the leading guard is accidental protection, not a gate, and an operator cannot tell 'did not run' from 'found nothing'. With the bare SEX declared the run reports SKIPPED instead. Verdict 2-1' per CORE-RULES-AUTHORING-GUIDELINES 4.4; the absence is reported by the universal PMDA-AD0047 (not contains_all($dataset_variables, $required_variables)), which is present in all four rules-pmda-adamig packages. Note PMDA-AD0047 is LIBRARY-DEPENDENT while this gate is not, so on a run with no library metadata the discharge is inert and the gate still stands."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADSL
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col SAFFL   type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | Y
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | Y
---

dataset DM label=Demographics
col STUDYID type=Char
col DOMAIN  type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col SEX     type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 | F
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1023 | F
---
